{"schemaVersion":1,"kind":"error","classification":"planning","code":"PROMPT_CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED","message":"Headless execution requires clarification before a repository plan can be created.","promptUnderstanding":{"schemaVersion":1,"promptId":"7e2f3b059985b754d6119b0db3692cf27e2f3b059985b754d6119b0db3692cf2","inputId":"3435423d77742df4c8dc52dde3bcf53e3435423d77742df4c8dc52dde3bcf53e","outcome":"repository_action","readiness":"clarification_required","reply":"I can perform a read-only inspection to explain the runtime boundary and cite the supporting files. Before doing that, please confirm which runtime boundary you mean, because the request does not identify a component or entry point.","conversationSummary":"The user requests a read-only repository inspection explaining a runtime boundary with file citations. No repository path, component, or entry point has been identified. No edits are authorized; protected paths include .env, .git/**, and bun.lock. The user says to run bun test only when execution is appropriate.","refinedBrief":{"goal":"Explain one identified runtime boundary from the repository and cite the files that demonstrate it.","deliverables":["A concise explanation of the selected runtime boundary.","File citations showing the relevant entry points, interfaces, and execution path.","Read-only validation results if a relevant test can be run without expanding scope."],"constraints":["Read-only inspection only; do not modify repository contents.","Do not access or modify protected paths: .env, .git/**, or bun.lock.","Run bun test only if it is directly relevant to the selected boundary and can be run safely."],"acceptanceCriteria":["The explanation identifies the boundary, the components on each side, and the mechanism crossing it.","Each material claim is supported by cited repository files.","No files are changed."],"nonGoals":["Implementing, refactoring, or configuring the runtime.","Inspecting unrelated components.","Modifying protected paths."]},"questions":[{"id":"runtime_boundary_target","prompt":"Which runtime boundary should the read-only inspection cover?","rationale":"The repository target is necessary to determine which files and tests are relevant.","kind":"outcome","options":[{"id":"main_application","label":"Main application boundary","description":"Trace the primary application runtime entry point and its boundary to supporting processes or services.","recommended":true},{"id":"cli_boundary","label":"CLI boundary","description":"Trace the command-line entry point and its boundary to the application runtime.","recommended":false},{"id":"named_component","label":"Named component","description":"Inspect a specific component or subsystem you identify in a free-form reply.","recommended":false}]}],"assumptions":[]}}
